# Who is asked to review what.
#
# GitHub requests these reviewers automatically. It is a routing table, not a
# permission system — it decides who is ASKED, and branch protection decides who
# must approve.
#
# Only handles that are known to be real are listed. An owner entry pointing at a
# username that does not exist, or at a team nobody is in, silently requests
# nobody: the pull request then looks reviewed-by-design and is reviewed by
# no one. Add a line when you know the handle, not before.

# Everything, by default.
*                                   @architinit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The parts where a mistake is not a bug but a breach. These carry the thirteen
# rules in CLAUDE.md, and every one of them is enforced by a test that a
# sufficiently determined change can also edit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Authorization. `decide()` is the object check, and it runs before content is
# read on every path.
/packages/conversation-domain/      @architinit

# Message visibility and the durability ordering — a message is durable before it
# is delivered, and a customer can never see an internal note.
/packages/messaging/                @architinit

# Schema, constraints and the namespace guard. The one-owner exclusion constraint
# and the append-only audit trigger live here; so does the guard that runs before
# the first connection.
/infrastructure/database/           @architinit

# The build's own gates. Weakening one of these is invisible in a green run,
# which is exactly why it needs a second pair of eyes.
/infrastructure/guards/             @architinit
/.github/workflows/                 @architinit
/.dependency-cruiser.cjs            @architinit
/vitest.config.ts                   @architinit
/vitest.workspace.ts                @architinit

# Configuration contracts: the SL_ prefix, no fallback chains, no shipped
# production defaults.
/.env.example                       @architinit

# The documents the code is answerable to.
/docs/                              @architinit
/CLAUDE.md                          @architinit
